       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high. At that level the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. Here are some options:\n- **Usual starting dose:** 5 mg orally once daily.\n- **Frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment:** 2.5 mg orally once daily.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg orally once daily.\n\nIf you tell me the dose you want, I'll enter it right away. If you meant to treat uncontrolled hypertension, adding a second agent from another class is usually preferred over going above 10 mg of amlodipine. I can enter that order too."
